    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 264 tests pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, with 0 failures and 0 errors. The `ERROR` log line about `POST /api/users` is from a pre-existing negative-path test (it asserts the error handling), not a failure.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `riskFlag` field on the owner response so it returns `true` when **any** of the three risk signals hold, and `false` otherwise.\n\n**OpenAPI schema** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a `riskFlag` boolean property to the `Owner` schema (which generates `OwnerDto` at build time), documenting the three conditions.\n\n**Controller** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`) \u2014 added the risk logic and wired `ownerDto.setRiskFlag(isRiskFlag(owner))` into the same three response paths that already set `capacityWarning`: `getOwner`, the idempotent-return path, and the create path.\n\nThe three conditions, matching the spec:\n1. **Possible duplicate** \u2014 reuses the owner's persisted `possibleDuplicate` flag (`Boolean.TRUE.equals(...)`).\n2. **Disposable-adjacent email domain** \u2014 a new `isDisposableAdjacentEmail` helper: true when the email's domain is exactly a known disposable domain, a subdomain of one, or shares its second-level label with one (e.g. `mailinator.com` is disposable, so `mailinator.net`/`mail.mailinator.io` are *adjacent*). Exact disposable domains are already rejected at create time, so this widens the net to the near-misses that a create otherwise accepts. `null` email \u2192 false.\n3. **City over soft capacity** \u2014 `isOverSoftCapacity` reuses the existing `CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD` (40); true when the city holds \u2265 40 owners.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreRiskFlagFalseNormally` (a fully-unique owner: no duplicate, no email, unique city) correctly reports `riskFlag: false`.",
